Got through the quest to the bottom.  (Still there killing things.)
Used tricks for getting rid of the trolls (lock them in the handy
rooms, kill them then run up/down the stairs and wait until the body
demcomposes (is this a bug?)).  Got down to the bottom level, and
Thoth Amon was a wimp.  Went looking around, wading through ogre
corpses, something appears beside me, hit it, Thoth Amon gasps his
last breaths.

The bottom level of the Barbarian quest is sacrifice heaven.  You get an
altar and all the monsters that come out are ogres and trolls.  They
almost always leave corpses, carry lots of wands (mostly teleportation),
and are 'smart'.

Start with a wand or two of create monster and you're self sufficient.
Pile junk on the altar and zap away.  Move around a bit and the monsters
(except ogre kings, not sure why) will move toward you, and try to get
on the altar to pick things up (convenient).  Kill, #offer, look for
stuff they left behind, repeat ad nauseum.  Make sure you have reflection
(or a suitably low ac) as a couple of them have had wands of death.


